<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guglielmo Boccanegra</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1274">1274</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Guglielmo Boccanegra (died 1274) was a Genoese merchant leader who became the first Captain of the People of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a> in 1257 after a popular revolt against the nobility. He negotiated the Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nymphaion">Nymphaeum</a> with the Byzantine emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michael-viii-palaiologos">Michael VIII Palaiologos</a> in 1261, but his authoritarian rule provoked the nobles, who overthrew him in 1262 and restored their own control of the commune.</p></div>
